body:
When the support for event processing metrics was added to the `TcpSource` framework (#9540), tests were added to all relevant sources to ensure they continued to operate properly. Unfortunately, two of the sources, `fluent` and `logstash` sources, do not work with the test framework, and the tests were removed in #9576.

As far as I can determine, theses sources _are_ emitting the appropriate events in the `TcpSource` implementation just like the others (verified by `dbg` statements), however the component test handler is not receiving the events and macros. This suggests that something in the sources may be introducing threading, which is known to break the component test hander, but I am unable to see what might be causing this behavior.

@jszwedko I am adding you to the assigned list as you appear to have written these sources and might have some other insights.

### A note for the community

I am using filebeat from elasticsearch with the elastic common schema. 
I try to addopt vector as the new logshipper.  

vectroy allready adds some metada to the sink logs like hostmeta data. 

is there a easy setup for add some meta data about the agent itself. For example 

```proto
message Agent {
  message Build {
    string original = 1;
  }

  Build build = 1;
  string ephemeral_id = 2;
  string id = 3;
  string name = 4;
  string type = 5;
  string version = 6;
}
```
